# For more info on HTTP files go to https://aka.ms/vs/httpfile
@api = https://localhost:7001/api

### 1. Log in as the demo customer. The next requests reuse this token automatically.
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "priya@example.com",
  "password": "Kiyaara123"
}

### 2. Who am I? (sends the token)
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 3. Priya's own orders (KY-1003 is hers)
GET {{api}}/orders/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 4. The same without a token: 401 Unauthorized
GET {{api}}/orders/mine

### 5. Wrong password: 401 Unauthorized
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "priya@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpass1"
}

### 6. Create a new account (the second time: 400, email already exists)
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Meera Joshi",
  "email": "meera@example.com",
  "mobile": "9876543210",
  "password": "Kiyaara2026"
}

### 7. Weak password: 400 with the password rule
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "mobile": "9876543211",
  "password": "short"
}

### 8. Place an order as Priya (201 Created, and it appears in request 3)
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "items": [ { "productId": 11, "size": "Free Size", "quantity": 1 } ],
  "address": {
    "fullName": "Priya Nair", "mobile": "9847012345", "pincode": "682011",
    "city": "Kochi", "state": "Kerala", "house": "14/2 Marine Drive Road",
    "area": "Ernakulam", "landmark": "", "addressType": "Home"
  },
  "paymentMethod": "COD"
}

### 9. Forgot password: look in the API console window for the reset link
POST {{api}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "priya@example.com"
}

  @api = https://localhost:7001/api

### 1. The demo admin signs in (Asha). Requests below reuse this token.
# @name admin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@kiyaara.com",
  "password": "Admin2026"
}

### 2. Priya signs in (a shopper)
# @name shopper
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "priya@example.com",
  "password": "Kiyaara123"
}

### 3. Every order, as the admin: 200 OK
GET {{api}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.token}}

### 4. Every order, as Priya: 403 Forbidden (logged in, but not an admin)
GET {{api}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{shopper.response.body.$.token}}

### 5. Every order, with no token: 401 Unauthorized (not logged in)
GET {{api}}/orders

### 6. Dashboard, as the admin: 200 OK
GET {{api}}/dashboard/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.token}}

### 7. Priya opens her own order KY-1003: 200 OK
GET {{api}}/orders/1003
Authorization: Bearer {{shopper.response.body.$.token}}

### 8. Priya opens someone else's order KY-1001: 404 Not Found
GET {{api}}/orders/1001
Authorization: Bearer {{shopper.response.body.$.token}}

### 9. The product list is still open to everyone: 200 OK
GET {{api}}/products

### 10. Priya tries to delete a product: 403 Forbidden (nothing is deleted)
DELETE {{api}}/products/12
Authorization: Bearer {{shopper.response.body.$.token}}
